.fo off

DISKPRY - A command to allow one to snoop around on an EDF format CMS
          minidisk. Can be used to learn how disks are organized, or
          to diagnose what is wrong with a minidisk. Can be used to
          rewrite actual disk blocks and create a disk file from
          data in disk blocks.


Format:   DISKPRY fm

    Note: "fm" is the filemode for an ACCESSed disk. This disk must be
           EDF format.

Operation: DISKPRY will type the location or value for various interesting
           things for the disk, such as the location of the ADT entry,
           the location of the directory, etc.

           Next you are asked if you want to have the directory entries
           typed at the terminal. This will include the file origin
           pointer(1st block number) for each file, and the number of
           pointer levels for the file.

           Next you will prompted for a command:

           Command:(READ|WRITE|MAP|EXIT|FOP|SCAN|SAVE|CMS|COPY)

           Where:    READ  - Read a disk block. You will br prompted
                             for the number of the block to be read
                             into the disk block buffer.

                     WRITE - Rewrite last block read from disk block
                             buffer.

                     MAP   - List disk directory.

                     EXIT  - Leave DISKPRY, return to CMS.

                     FOP   - Return the file origin pointer for a
                             specified file.

                     SCAN  - Scan all blocks on the minidisk for
                             a specified string. Can be used to locate
                             data blocks of files that have been ERASEd.
                             It is possible to scan for fullword binary
                             values, or character strings.

                     SAVE  - Record the data currently in the disk block
                             buffer in the file "DISKPRY SAVEFILE A".
                             Can be used to recreate an ERASEd file.

                     CMS   - Enter CMS SUBSET.

                     COPY  - Copy input minidisk block-by-block to
                             another RW ACCESSed minidisk. Output
                             minidisk will become an exact copy of the
                             input minidisk. Bad input blocks will be
                             skipped. Can be used to recover a minidisk
                             from a bad HDA.

    Note:  "WRITE" will rewrite the last block read. This command
           should be used with caution.

           "COPY" will rewrite the output minidisk entirely. Use
           also with caution.

